  "preamble": "Fronting and slight lowering of the close central unrounded [ɨ] to near-close near-front [ɪ]. In Ukrainian the Old East Slavic vowels ы [ɨ] (from Proto-Slavic *y) and и [i] merged into one sound [ɪ], written и, and the letter ы was given up; Ukrainian [i], written і, comes from other sources. Ukrainian thus has син [sɪn] 'son' and дим [dɪm] 'smoke' where Russian and Belarusian keep ы [ɨ].",
  "phoneticEffects": "Fronting, Lowering, Merger",
